WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.258
ALEX: So. Thirty-five billion dollars in
a single stock offering. Meta filed this

00:00:03.258 --> 00:00:06.517
ALEX: today. Walk me through the
structure, because it isn't just one big

00:00:06.517 --> 00:00:09.775
ALEX: pile of shares.

00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:14.243
RUFUS: Two tranches. About twenty-two-
and-a-half billion in Class A common
stock — the

00:00:14.243 --> 00:00:18.600
RUFUS: regular shares. And then another
twelve-and-a-half billion in depositary
shares representing mandatory

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.958
RUFUS: convertible preferred stock.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.722
JAMIE: What's the preferred stock doing
there?

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:29.395
RUFUS: Investors get a fixed return for
a period, then the shares automatically

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:32.982
RUFUS: convert into common stock. It
lets Meta attract people who want a

00:00:32.982 --> 00:00:36.570
RUFUS: bit more downside protection
without issuing bonds.
